## What Loads, and When

| Loaded every session, unconditionally | Loaded only when something reads it |
|---|---|
| `CLAUDE.md` (this file) · `.claude/rules/*.md` | `.claude/docs/*` · `memory/*` · skill bodies |

What follows from that:

- **Every line here and in `.claude/rules/` is paid for on each turn.** Keep this file under 100 lines and each rule file under ~60. Detail belongs in `.claude/docs/`.
- **Skills and agents are auto-discovered.** Their names and descriptions are already in context — listing them here duplicates what the harness supplies and goes stale the moment one is added. Don't.
- **Hooks are not discoverable.** Nothing tells you what runs automatically, so the hook table below is the only inventory that exists. Keep it accurate.
- Everything else is lazy by design: read it at the moment of need, not in advance.

---

## Read When

| Situation | File |
|---|---|
| Session start, current priorities | `memory/state/dashboard.md` |
| Working on a project | `memory/projects/[project]/context.md` |
| Hit an error | `memory/knowledge/errors.md` |
| Recording a learning | `memory/knowledge/learnings.md` |
| How the memory system works | `.claude/docs/memory-system.md` |
| Scoring a plan or research output | `.claude/docs/quality-gates.md` |
| Worked examples of asking vs acting | `.claude/docs/decision-protocol.md` |
| Setting up recurring checks | `.claude/docs/loop-integration.md` |

Decision protocol, communication style and verification discipline live in `.claude/rules/` — already loaded, no read needed.

`memory/state/` is current and gets rewritten; `memory/knowledge/` accumulates; `memory/projects/` is per-project; `memory/daily/` gets one file per session at `/end`.

